new-page: true

> *"The oligarchy will not give up its privileges voluntarily. The latifundiários will not surrender their lands voluntarily. The imperialists will not leave Brazil voluntarily. Therefore we must prepare — seriously, patiently, without illusions — for the struggle that is coming."*

— PCdoB founding documents, 1962

This is a game of alternate history set in the most convulsive decade of Brazilian politics. The history is rendered as faithfully as possible — the figures, the factions, the betrayals, and the blood are real. But this is still a game, and you may find paths that history did not take. The author welcomes corrections.

The PCdoB in February 1962 is a party of perhaps a few hundred active cadres, operating in clandestinity under a government that tolerates us only so long as we are useful. We have broken with the PCB and with Moscow. We look to Mao, to Havana, to the landless laborers of the Northeast and the forests of the Araguaia. The question before us is not *whether* the ruling class will resort to force — it will, it always does — but whether we will be ready when it does.

We were not ready in 1964. This is your chance to change that.

For background on Brazilian politics, parties, and the history of the communist movement, see the Library. First-time players are strongly encouraged to read it.

